{
  "summary": "The UI generally follows the spec and passes automated accessibility (axe 0 violations, Lighthouse 98 % a11y) and the primary flow test covers all major screens. However, several secondary states required by the DESIGN.md are not exercised or appear to be missing in the codebase (error, loading, empty, validation, offline, and generation states). These omissions are medium‑severity gaps because they affect resilience and completeness of the user experience but don’t break the primary happy‑path flow. No hard‑coded colors or sizes were detected, and the components appear to use the provided design tokens. Focus outlines and touch‑target sizes look correct, but a few accessibility details (focus‑visible on custom dialogs, explicit `role=\"alertdialog\"` for the Delete‑All‑Data confirmation, and `aria-live` on the Snackbar) could be reinforced. Overall the app is solid, but the missing secondary UI states and a handful of small accessibility polish items need attention before the product can be considered fully finished.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/DashboardScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Missing error state view with the copy “Failed to load data. Pull down to retry.” – the DESIGN.md specifies an error screen with a Retry button, but no such UI component or logic is present.",
      "fix": "Add a full‑screen error component that displays the required message and a PrimaryButton labeled “Retry” which re‑triggers data loading. Ensure it uses the `ErrorView` pattern and design tokens for colors and spacing."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/ReceiptsScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Empty state for receipts (title: “No receipts recorded”, description, primary button “Add receipt”) is not referenced in the source. The screen only renders the list or loading spinner.",
      "fix": "Render the `EmptyState` component when `receipts.length === 0` and pass the exact copy strings. Wire the primary button to open the FAB (or navigate to the receipt entry flow)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/MileageScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Missing empty‑state view for mileage (title: “No mileage logged”). The spec calls for this but the code only shows an empty list.",
      "fix": "Add the `EmptyState` component with the required title, description, and primary action “Add mileage” when there are no mileage entries."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/ReceiptEntryScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Validation error UI (HelperText under each field) is not present in the component implementation; fields only display generic error states.",
      "fix": "Integrate the `HelperText type=\"error\"` component under each `FormField` and display the exact validation messages from `src/lib/validation.ts`. Ensure the Save button stays disabled until all fields are valid."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/MileageEntryScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Same as above – per‑field validation messages and disabled Save button are not implemented.",
      "fix": "Add `HelperText` error messages for Miles, Date, and Purpose fields, and keep the Save button disabled until validation passes."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/SettingsScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Settings error state (Snackbar with “Unable to load settings.”) is not rendered anywhere; the screen assumes data loads successfully.",
      "fix": "Wrap the settings load in a try/catch and display a `Snackbar` with the required copy on failure."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/TaxSettingsScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Missing validation error UI for the mileage‑rate and tax‑rate fields, and missing disabled Save button until a change occurs.",
      "fix": "Show `HelperText type=\"error\"` with the generic validation message when a field value is out‑of‑range. Enable the Save button only after the user modifies a field."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/ExportScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Export‑running state (buttons disabled with spinner and copy “Generating export…”) is not implemented; the UI allows repeated taps during export.",
      "fix": "Add local state `exportRunning` that disables both Export CSV and Export PDF buttons, shows a small `ActivityIndicator` inside each button, and displays the required copy while the export promise is pending."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/BackupScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Backup generation state (full‑screen ActivityIndicator with the copy “Creating encrypted backup…”) is missing; the UI only shows a button.",
      "fix": "When the user confirms the passphrase, render a full‑screen overlay with the `ActivityIndicator` and the required copy until the backup is created."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
